--- changes required to make it build -----------------------------

Files that needed NO change (compiled as delivered):
  Anchors.lean       — already carried the grind fix from paper-079
  LocalClosure.lean  — byte-identical to the paper-079 version
  LocalClosure2.lean — new; kernel 'decide' over 343 + 625 lock
                       cubes, ~8s, axiom-free

[1] Certificate.lean — 1 error: 'cert_nonneg' (was 'by grind')

      error: Certificate.lean:44:2: `grind` failed
      h : ¬0 ≤ ((x - 27*50⁻¹)*(x - 263*200⁻¹)*(x - 103*50⁻¹))^2

    Cause: grind's ring/linarith core treats '(...)^2' as an
    OPAQUE ATOM. Its own diagnostics show it guessing the atom
    value ('[assign] 「(...)^2」 := 4') rather than knowing the
    term is a square. So a perfect-square nonnegativity goal is
    outside what 'grind' can do, in this and any future file.

    Fix: core Lean DOES ship the ordered-ring lemma
      Lean.Grind.OrderedRing.sq_nonneg   {a : R} : 0 ≤ a^2
        (Init/Grind/Ordered/Ring.lean:366)
    and Init/Grind/Ordered/Rat.lean supplies the Rat instance.
    'cert_nonneg' is now a term-mode proof by that lemma.
    Still mathlib-free. Statement unchanged.

[2] SOSCertificate.lean — did not compile at all, and was NOT
    listed in lakefile roots, so 'lake build' silently skipped it.
    Its header said 'toolchain compile pending'. It was written
    against mathlib despite claiming 'core-only':

      * 'ℚ'        -> unknown identifier in core Lean 4.33
                      (core suggests 'Rat'); every downstream
                      HSub/HMul/HPow instance error cascaded
                      from this one unknown identifier
      * 'ring'     -> unknown tactic (mathlib)
      * 'norm_num' -> mathlib (5 occurrences)
      * 'sq_nonneg'-> mathlib

    Fix (purely mechanical, NO numeral changed):
      ℚ -> Rat ; ring -> grind ; norm_num -> grind ;
      sq_nonneg _ -> Lean.Grind.OrderedRing.sq_nonneg
    Added 'SOSCertificate' to lakefile roots so the build now
    actually covers every .lean file in the directory.
    Header STATUS updated (it is no longer 'compile pending',
    and the CDN-unreachable note no longer applies).

